    "durationMs": 193894,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Everything was tested end-to-end through the exact `sh start.sh` path the harness will use.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `database/migrations/2025_01_01_000000_create_links_table.php` — `links` table with `text` url, case-sensitive `utf8mb4_bin` unique `code` varchar(20), and `clicks` counter\n- `app/Models/Link.php` — Eloquent model with integer click cast\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — all four endpoints with the exact status contract (201 create, 409 duplicate, 404 unknown, 422 validation incl. malformed JSON), atomic `clicks + 1` increment, URL stored and returned verbatim, and a unique-index race backstop for duplicate codes\n- `routes/api.php` + `bootstrap/app.php` — registered with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are `/links` and `/r/{code}` (no `/api` prefix, no CSRF/session middleware, no rate limiting)\n- `start.sh` (executable) — `php artisan migrate --force` then `php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` with 4 workers\n- README section covering startup and the endpoint table\n\n**Verified via curl against the running server:** generated codes are unique alphanumeric, all invalid url/code variants return 422 with an `error` field, redirects return 302 with the exact stored Location, clicks increment exactly once per redirect, list is in ascending creation order with `total`, and — after killing and restarting the server — all links and click counts survived (clicks continued from 2 to 3). Codes are case-sensitive, Pint passes, the starter test suite passes, and I left the database empty and port 8000 free for the grader."
  }
